{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Revise the school mobile phone legislation for KS5 students (aged 16 and above)",
        "additional_details": "We are concerned that this ban could have a serious negative effect on the performance of students. Whilst overall the ban could be beneficial to a school environment, we think it creates problems for KS5 students (aged 16-18). This is because in a digital age, most resources for independent study are online. Allowing KS5 students more freedom could improve performance and results. \r\n \r\nWe also think it is unfair to confiscate a 17 or 18 year olds phone. These are people who are near adulthood.",
        "background": "We think the new legislation banning mobile phones in school should be revised to cater to KS5 students (aged 16-18). We believe these students need the freedom to endeavour in self study without being restricted by phone bans.",
